=== Routing policy ===
# Model-Routing Policy

**Assumption:** per-call token counts aren't in the summary, so I use the per-model average (Fable: ~5,490 tok/call, ~$0.109/call at your observed ~75% input / 25% output mix). Haiku's pricing is exactly 1/10 of Fable's and 1/2 of Sonnet's, Sonnet's is 1/5 of Fable's — so the savings ratios hold regardless of mix.

## Routing tiers

| Tier | Model | Belongs here | Why (one-sentence test) |
|---|---|---|---|
| Cheap | **Haiku** | typo_fix, rename_variable, one_line_summary, log_triage, answer_slack_question | Mechanical, single-path tasks — no branches, no judgment, just execute or look up. |
| Mid | **Sonnet** | implement_diff, fix_one_test, mcp_audit_execute | Scoped code changes with some reasoning (why is the test failing? does the diff fit the codebase?), but one bounded problem. |
| Premium | **Fable** | threat_model, migration_plan | Open-ended, multi-branch, consequential planning where a wrong call is expensive to unwind. |

## Mis-routed calls this week (5 of 12)

All on Fable at ~$0.109/call:

| Task | Was on | Should be | New cost | Savings/call |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| typo_fix | Fable | **Haiku** | ~$0.011 | **~$0.098** |
| rename_variable | Fable | **Haiku** (you already routed another one there — the policy exists, just inconsistently applied) | ~$0.011 | **~$0.098** |
| one_line_summary | Fable | **Haiku** | ~$0.011 | **~$0.098** |
| answer_slack_question | Fable | **Haiku** (it's a lookup-and-reply; escalate to Sonnet only if it requires reading code) | ~$0.011 | **~$0.098** |
| fix_one_test | Fable | **Sonnet** (needs diagnosis, so not Haiku — but it's one bounded fix, not a plan) | ~$0.022 | **~$0.087** |

**Correctly routed:** threat_model and migration_plan on Fable (genuine judgment/branching); both implement_diff calls and mcp_audit_execute on Sonnet; rename_variable and log_triage on Haiku.

## Bottom line

- Estimated weekly savings: **~$0.48 of your $0.88 spend (~55%)**.
- Fable drops from 7 calls to 2; your premium model was doing typo fixes 71% of the time.
- Projected spend under policy: Fable ~$0.22, Sonnet ~$0.14, Haiku ~$0.05 → **~$0.41/week**.

**Policy in one line:** default every task to Haiku; promote to Sonnet only if the task requires diagnosing *why* something is wrong; promote to Fable only if the output is a plan with branches and tradeoffs rather than a change.

